sd: run DrawController::select from other threads on the main thread.

Deadlock seen on Windows (Draw, after a table edit, a UNO client's select() from its bridge thread):
the bridge thread holds the ViewShellManager mutex while the new selection context builds a sidebar
panel; VCL creates the native window on the main thread through SendMessage with the SolarMutex
released; the main thread takes the SolarMutex, runs a dispatcher slot that needs the
ViewShellManager mutex, and the bridge thread can no longer get the SolarMutex back.
Hook: two lines in DrawController::select forward to sd::hst::selectOnMainThread (HST-owned header,
vcl::solarthread::syncExecute, the upstream sfx2 idiom). select and getSelection also take the
SolarMutex before the disposed check.

License: HstControllerMainThread.hxx is HST-owned (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); DrawController.cxx
keeps MPL-2.0.
Test: CppunitTest_sd_a11y (HstControllerSelectThread).
